WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.582
Each food test detects one nutrient. Benedict's solution tests for reducing sugar. A reducing sugar is a simple sugar, such as glucose. This test must be heated in a water bath. Iodine tests for starch. Biuret tests for protein.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:28.888
Ethanol and then water test for lipid. DCPIP tests for vitamin C. Learn the positive colour, and the negative colour, for every test.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:44.320
Here is a sample, X. Step one: for each test, write the nutrient it detects. Benedict's for sugar. Iodine for starch. Biuret for protein.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:55.305
Step two: turn each colour into present or absent. Brick red: sugar is present. Yellow-brown: no starch. Blue: no protein.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:10.224
Step three: combine the readings to answer the question. Sample X contains reducing sugar, but no starch and no protein. If a question gives a colour, use it to name the reagent: blue-black means iodine.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:29.920
Tests are also used with Visking tubing. Visking tubing is a bag with tiny holes. Starch molecules are too large to pass through. Glucose is small enough to pass out. So the water outside gives a positive Benedict's test, but a negative iodine test.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:43.380
Now a real exam question. Three food tests are done on one food solution. Describe what the tests show. Three marks.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:52.157
Here is the table. Iodine solution gave blue-black. Biuret solution gave purple. Benedict's solution stayed blue.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:59.951
Take them one at a time. Iodine turned blue-black. Iodine tests for starch, so starch is present.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:04.936
Biuret turned purple. Biuret tests for protein, so protein is present.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:15.435
Benedict's stayed blue. Blue is the negative result. So there is no reducing sugar. This is the mark most students miss.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.032
Here is the full answer. It is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:34.196
A common mistake is to say blue after Benedict's means sugar. Blue is the colour it starts with. So blue means no sugar.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:42.846
Another mistake is to list only the nutrients that are present. A negative result is a result too. Write it.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:03:01.981
Your turn. Three powders, P, Q and R, are tested with iodine and biuret. P gives yellow-brown and lilac. Q gives blue-black and blue. R gives blue-black and lilac. Which powders contain protein but no starch? Pause here and work it out.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:15.370
Turn each colour into present or absent. P: no starch, protein. Q: starch, no protein. R: starch and protein.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:24.542
Now combine the two conditions. Only P has protein but no starch. R has protein, but it also has starch.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:35.259
So, every time: say what each test detects. Turn every colour into present or absent. Then combine the readings to answer the question.
